Nephi Allred wrote:
> I've decided to work on an idea that has been kicked around a lot: making
> some of the crappier artifacts more desirable.

yay! Be careful, though. They need to be more powerful, but not too
much, imho. They should remain very monster specific, rather than being
too generically useful.

> For all banes: warning for target monster (like Sting for orcs).

Definitely yes. I think this is a must.

> Giantslayer: grant 25 strength? (I don't really like this idea because I
> think that the banes shouldn't give the powers of the monsters they
> fight, but I can't think of anything else.)

I don't see anything wrong with this. After all, if you're up against a
strong opponent, you'd want to be strong to to fight them. However,
there might be alternatives:

[Your post re-arranged somewhat]
> Giantslayer: something to do with "seven in one blow". Maybe if the
> player is surrounded by giants, s/he has a small chance to kill them all
> with one hit.

Ooohhh... obscure, but kind of nice. Another useful ability WRT giants
would be some way of helping you eat them all without choking. Either
some kind of giant-tinning ability (You see here a giant fillet), or
magical breathing while eating giant corpses, or make their corpses
unperishable or... something.

Another idea: How about some kind of defence against thrown boulders?
When a giant throws a boulder at you (or when one comes at you from a
rolling boulder trap) and you are wielding Giantslayer, it smashes the
boulder to rubble before it can hit you. You could also use it to smash
up stationary boulders, by (a)pplying it as you would a pickaxe. If it
could do statues as well, that would definitely be handy.

> Dragonbane: reflection. I don't think this is unbalancing given that the
